  "subject": "Four implementer-execution fixes from an adopter-org field report (edgreenlight, Director-relayed 2026-08-24), all strategist-verified against the repo, ranked: (1) DATA-LOSS HAZARD -- install-claude-code-skills.ps1 does Remove-Item -Recurse -Force on a junction before recreating it, which on PowerShell 5.1 can traverse into the user's clone and delete their skill sources; re-run-after-git-pull is the documented normal workflow so it sits on the likely path; NOT reproduced by either the reporter or me, so reproduce on 5.1 first; the .sh sibling is safe (rm -rf on a POSIX symlink removes the link); (2) README Status block is stale in a misinforming way -- not just a version number, it tells adopters the seat identifiers, GitHub org and oagp.org rename is still pending when v0.2.1 completed it twelve weeks ago; (3) stale 'cd oagp-org' strings in both installer headers, cosmetic only (the README's documented path is correct -- the reporter self-corrected this one); (4) agent-sdk/examples/bind_time_travel.py:23 hardcodes s:/projects/thingalog, the ONLY live stale path in the tree -- the other 137 hits are dated records in memos/, transcripts/ and charter history[] and MUST NOT be swept (retro-editing records is the same error as retro-rebranding). Explicitly NOT in scope for this memo: the operations-addressability proposal and the skill-suite rename/merge -- both reach you later as ratified decisions; do not pre-emptively edit the installer $skills arrays.",

  "sent": "2026-08-24T14:22:00-04:00",
  "action_required": true,

  "body": "Four verified implementer-execution items from an adopter-org field report relayed by the Director on 2026-08-24. Origin: a Claude session inside edgreenlight (non-spec real org, OG-shaped via /og-create 2026-06-12) lost its OG skills in a machine reorganization, investigated, and reported back unbriefed and with no stake in the outcome. Every claim strategist-verified against the repo before filing; overstatements and understatements both called out. ITEM 1 (fix first, data-loss hazard): install/install-claude-code-skills.ps1:44 runs Remove-Item -Recurse -Force on an existing skill entry that :48 created as a directory junction via mklink /J. On PowerShell 5.1 that can traverse the junction and delete the target's contents -- the user's clone of this repo, i.e. their skill sources. PowerShell 7 handles it correctly. It sits on the likely path because the README documents git pull + re-run as the normal update workflow, and re-running is exactly when the Remove-Item branch fires. NOT reproduced by the reporter or by me: reproduce on 5.1 before fixing, and if it does not reproduce, say so and we close it rather than carrying a phantom. Candidate shapes (implementation is implementer's call): (Get-Item $dst).Delete(); or test the ReparsePoint attribute and branch; or cmd /c rmdir. The .sh sibling is SAFE -- rm -rf on a POSIX symlink removes the link not the target -- and that asymmetry should be stated in the reply. ITEM 2: README.md:9 Status block is stale in a way that misinforms adopters -- it is not merely a v0.2.0/v0.2.1 version drift as reported, it actively tells the reader that the seat identifiers, the GitHub repo/org name and oagp.org 'remain on their legacy names pending a coordinated rename follow-on', when v0.2.1 completed that follow-on on 2026-06-01. The repo's front door describes a half-finished migration that finished twelve weeks ago, to an audience deciding whether to adopt. Rewrite to current fact and audit the rest of the README against the same question. ITEM 3: stale 'cd oagp-org' in both installer usage headers and both error strings (4 occurrences); the clone dir is 'og'. Cosmetic -- the reporter initially called it the place adopters follow instructions literally, then checked and self-corrected: the README Quick-install path is correct, so nobody on the documented path hits it. Fix in passing; not a defect. ITEM 4: agent-sdk/examples/bind_time_travel.py:23 hardcodes Path('s:/projects/thingalog'), broken since the Director's projects moved to s:/projects-personal. This is the ONLY live stale path in the tree: a full sweep found 137 hits, of which 99 are in memos/, plus transcripts/ and the charter's history[]/staffed_via prose -- all dated records of where work actually happened, which MUST NOT be swept (retro-editing records is the same error as retro-rebranding OAGP->OG, settled policy). Make the example relative or env-driven; the house pattern already exists at channels/src/memo-watch-channel.js:30 (OG_MEMOS_DIR with a __dirname-relative default). SCOPE: all four are implementer-execution with no embedded pattern-shape call; propose, Director ratifies, no merge from either seat. NOT IN THIS MEMO: the reporter's largest finding ('the substrate is durable, but the operations are a symlink') is pattern-shape and stays with the strategist -- it is becoming an operations-addressability proposal (an org declares which canonical operations it depends on and where they resolve from; operating discipline moves into the generated CLAUDE.md so guardrails survive the tooling going missing) and will arrive as a separate build directive. Likewise the Director-settled skill-suite rename/merge (og-create-org, og-describe-org, og-close-session, og-add-seat; og-adopt merged away with an alias retained) will arrive as a ratified decision with an install-script sync directive: do NOT pre-emptively edit the $skills arrays, sync once against a merged artifact rather than twice against a moving one.",
  "body_ref": "2026-08-24-1422--og-strategist--og-implementer--field-report-fixes-installer-hazard-readme-drift-stale-path.body.md",

